    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Catalan counties united under the counts of Barcelona, who were also kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-aragon">Aragon</a> from 1162.</li><li>Its Corts, Generalitat and merchant capital Barcelona made it one of the most commercial and parliamentary states of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>Revolts in 1640 and 1705 ended in defeat, and the Nueva Planta decree of 1716 abolished its institutions.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Taula de Canvi, founded by Barcelona’s city council in 1401, was one of the first public banks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>, holding deposits and handling the city’s finances.</p></aside>
    </section>

